Talon — Local AI. Inference is Ollama on 127.0.0.1 only. Never use cloud LLM APIs, ClinePass, OpenRouter, or web fetch.

Python
- Interpreter: this kit's `.venv\Scripts\python.exe` (pandas, numpy, SQLAlchemy, scikit-learn, Jupyter, ruff).
- Prefer that venv. Do not `pip install` OpenAI / Anthropic / Azure / Google cloud SDKs.
- For analysis: pandas + matplotlib/seaborn. Save figures and CSVs under the workspace `data\` folder.

SQL
- Default database: workspace `data\local.sqlite` (SQLite, on disk, no server).
- Use `sqlite3` or SQLAlchemy `sqlite:///data/local.sqlite`.
- Put reusable queries in `.sql` files. Do not send dumps to remote hosts.
- If the user has another local DB (SQL Server Express, Postgres on localhost), keep the connection string on 127.0.0.1 and never enable cloud sync.

Memory (do this without asking)
- Before repeating an approach, read `memory/INDEX.md`, `memory/WHAT_WORKED.md`, and `memory/FAILED.md` if they exist.
- After every task, without waiting for the user, update a data map under `memory/data-maps/` for any tabular/SQL file you touched (column names and types only — never cell values, names, or chart IDs).
- After every task, append one short lesson under `memory/lessons/` and a row on WHAT_WORKED or FAILED. Say what worked or what to never try again.
- A background process also writes these files. Do not skip your write; merge if a file already exists.
- PHI stays on this PC. Do not paste it into a browser or any cloud chat.

Code
- Write complete, runnable Python/SQL. Run it in the terminal and fix failures.
- No GitHub remotes, no gist, no Copilot.
